DECISIONS (and the clause they follow):
  1. Order-insensitive global parsing, so `status --json --runtime-dir D` and
     `--runtime-dir D status --json` both work. The ticket says the fixture "honours
     --runtime-dir/AFANCTL_RUNTIME_DIR"; T04 must be invoked with `--runtime-dir <tmp>`
     (T04 card). Real afanctl exposes the dir only via env (afanctl README "Environment").
  2. monitor-only/absent status documents are derived with jq from the two owned status
     fixtures (the ticket owns exactly status-observe/status-hold), producing
     afanctl.status.v1 shapes consistent with afanctl DESIGN Appendix B / omafan DESIGN §4.1.
  3. argv.log records the effective argv after clamping (`hold 4200`, `observe`, `curve`)
     and only on a successful write, so a rejected/failed write leaves no trace.
  4. `--version`/`-h` are exempt from the runtime-dir requirement (they touch nothing);
     every data verb refuses without one (ticket: "must refuse to run unless a runtime
     dir is given"). require_runtime_dir also refuses /run/afanctl, /sys, /etc, /usr and
     /run per WORKER hard rule 4.
  5. write_cmd also emits afanctl.cmd.v1 to $runtime_dir/cmd.json via mktemp+mv, mirroring
     afanctl DESIGN Appendix B, so T05 can assert what was requested.
  6. harness temp root is created at source time (a lazily-created root inside the
     command-substitution subshell of `new_tmpdir` would not survive in the caller);
     `summarize` prints `PASS n / FAIL m`, removes the root, and returns non-zero on any
     failure; assertions record and return 0 so suites keep running under `set -e`.

OPEN: none. No change is needed in a file owned by another ticket, so QUESTIONS.md was
      not touched.
